  "reason": "The two completed experiments show that switching the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l yielded a large +8.3% accuracy gain (0.632→0.715), establishing config_042 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) as the current best. The next most impactful untested dimension is the aggregation method: avgpool is a simple mean that discards spatial/positional structure, while transformer aggregation can capture richer cross-modal interactions and per-token relationships. Config_018 is a clean single-variable change from config_042 (only aggregation changes from avgpool→transformer), so any performance delta is directly attributable to the aggregation choice. With 7 experiments remaining, testing this high-leverage architectural component early will either confirm a new best to build on or rule out transformer aggregation, reducing uncertainty before committing further budget to RNA-encoder or fusion variants."
}

